		<dict>
			<key>WFWorkflowActionIdentifier</key>
			<string>is.workflow.actions.comment</string>
			<key>WFWorkflowActionParameters</key>
			<dict>
				<key>WFCommentActionText</key>
				<string>Sync ShortLibrary sends your whole Shortcuts library to the ShortLibrary app.
It starts a sync in ShortLibrary, gets every shortcut you have, reads each shortcut's name, identifier, folder, icon, action count, creation date and last modified date, and imports each one into ShortLibrary. Then it finishes the sync and shows ShortLibrary's summary as a notification.
Requires the ShortLibrary app to be installed.</string>
			</dict>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>WFWorkflowActionIdentifier</key>
			<string>is.workflow.actions.comment</string>
			<key>WFWorkflowActionParameters</key>
			<dict>
				<key>WFCommentActionText</key>
				<string>Shortcuts generated by Shortcuts Playground. May contain mistakes. Always check the shortcut's actions first.

This shortcut was created via the following user prompt:

&gt; Build a macOS/iOS Shortcut named exactly "Sync ShortLibrary". It feeds a third-party app (ShortLibrary, bundle id fm.beard.ShortLibrary) the user's whole Shortcuts library through the app's own App Intents.
&gt;
&gt; Required action sequence:
&gt; 1. Call the ShortLibrary App Intent `BeginLibrarySyncIntent` (no parameters).
&gt; 2. "Get My Shortcuts" (is.workflow.actions.getmyworkflows), all shortcuts, no folder filter.
&gt; 3. "Repeat with Each" over the result. Inside the loop, for the Repeat Item (a Shortcut):
&gt;    - Use "Get Details of Shortcut" (is.workflow.actions.properties.workflow) to get, as separate actions: Name, Folder, Icon, Action Count, Creation Date, Last Modified Date. Also Color if the action offers that detail; check the ToolKit metadata for the exact list of available detail names for the Shortcut content item and tell me which exist. Skip any that don't exist.
&gt;    - Call the ShortLibrary App Intent `ImportShortcutIntent` with these parameters (Swift property names, which are the parameter keys): `name` (String, required, the Name detail; if Name isn't a detail use the Repeat Item itself coerced to text), `folder` (String?, Folder detail), `actionCount` (Int?, Action Count detail), `icon` (IntentFile, image, Icon detail), `color` (String?, Color detail if it exists), `created` (Date?, Creation Date), `modified` (Date?, Last Modified Date).
&gt; 4. After the loop, call the ShortLibrary App Intent `FinishLibrarySyncIntent` (no parameters), then "Show Result"/notification with its output text is optional but nice.

Follow-up: Color is not a Shortcut detail, so it was dropped. Identifier was added and goes to the identifier parameter of Import Shortcut. Position uses Repeat Index so ShortLibrary keeps the library order. The result of Finish Library Sync is shown with Show Notification.</string>
			</dict>
		</dict>
